<section class="section section-join-how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="join-how">
      <p class="eyebrow">Membership</p>
      <h2>How to join the CNA</h2>
      <p class="join-how-lead">The CNA is a council of White Plains&rsquo; <strong>established neighborhood associations</strong> &mdash; a forum where organized neighborhoods share ideas, work with the City, and speak with one voice. It is not an organization individuals join on their own: your neighborhood takes part through its association, whose officers or representatives attend meetings, pay dues, and vote on CNA matters.</p>

      <div class="join-eligibility">
        <h3>Who can join</h3>
        <p>A neighborhood association is eligible to join the CNA once it has:</p>
        <ul class="join-criteria">
          <li>a recognized White Plains neighborhood it represents</li>
          <li>a bank account</li>
          <li>officer leadership (such as president, vice president, treasurer, and secretary)</li>
          <li>a board of members</li>
          <li>dues collected from its members</li>
          <li>regular, documented meetings</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Neighborhoods that have not formed an association yet are warmly encouraged to start one &mdash; the workshop guide further down this page shows how. CNA meetings are open to the public; the meeting schedule is shared with member associations rather than published publicly. Dues-paying member associations have the right to vote on CNA matters.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="join-steps">
        <li class="join-step">
          <span class="join-step-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div class="join-step-body">
            <h3>Find your neighborhood association</h3>
            <p>These are the member organizations of the CNA. Check whether your neighborhood already has one on our <a href="{{ '/neighborhoods/' | withPrefix }}">Neighborhoods</a> page.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="join-step">
          <span class="join-step-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div class="join-step-body">
            <h3>Become a member of it</h3>
            <p>Join your local association and pay its dues. That is how residents take part &mdash; there is no separate individual CNA membership for the general public.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="join-step">
          <span class="join-step-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div class="join-step-body">
            <h3>No association yet? Start one</h3>
            <p>Use the workshop guide below to adopt bylaws, elect officers, and hold a first meeting. WPCNA will help you get going.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="join-step">
          <span class="join-step-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
          <div class="join-step-body">
            <h3>Your association joins the council</h3>
            <p>Once organized, your association pays its CNA dues and sends representatives to the council&rsquo;s monthly meetings &mdash; the second Tuesday of the month at 7:00 pm, in person or on Zoom.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="join-step">
          <span class="join-step-num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
          <div class="join-step-body">
            <h3>Add your voice</h3>
            <p>Attend meetings, share ideas, and connect with City officials and other neighborhoods across White Plains.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <aside class="join-note">
        <p><strong>Membership is for neighborhood associations and their members &mdash; not individual sign-ups from the general public.</strong> If your neighborhood is not organized yet, the guide below shows you how to change that.</p>
      </aside>

      <p class="join-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ '/contact/' | withPrefix }}">Questions about joining or dues? Contact the CNA</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="handbook-content">
      <article class="about-copy">
        <h2>{{ site.handbookIntroHeading }}</h2>
        {{ site.handbookIntroBody | paragraphs | safe }}

        <h3>What&rsquo;s inside the workshop guide</h3>
        <p>The deck below is a practical playbook for starting and running a neighborhood association, distilled from WPCNA&rsquo;s March 2025 workshop. Here is what it covers &mdash; so you can find what you need without sitting through the whole presentation:</p>
        <ul class="workshop-topics">
          <li><strong>The CNA &amp; the City</strong> &mdash; how neighborhood associations work with White Plains officials and the Common Council, and why an organized neighborhood carries a stronger voice.</li>
          <li><strong>Writing your bylaws</strong> &mdash; using Robert&rsquo;s Rules of Order as a ready-made template, then tailoring it to your neighborhood&rsquo;s needs.</li>
          <li><strong>Officers &amp; board</strong> &mdash; the four core roles (President, Vice President, Treasurer, Secretary) plus a board of roughly 10&ndash;15 members.</li>
          <li><strong>Holding elections</strong> &mdash; how to nominate and vote in officers at an annual meeting, with a simple ~60-day timeline.</li>
          <li><strong>Recruiting volunteers</strong> &mdash; practical ways to find, welcome, and keep neighbors involved.</li>
          <li><strong>Dues &amp; budgeting</strong> &mdash; setting dues, building a yearly budget, and tracking income and expenses (including the association&rsquo;s CNA dues).</li>
          <li><strong>Becoming a nonprofit (optional)</strong> &mdash; the three steps to form a 501(c)(7) social club in New York, plus the basic tax filings.</li>
          <li><strong>Events, meetings &amp; communication</strong> &mdash; planning and publicizing neighborhood events, and running consistent, well-organized meetings.</li>
        </ul>

        {% for resource in site.handbookResources %}
